Subject: Tensor-parallel DFlash2: sharded LM-head top-k, TP sharing strategy, lazy host page tier

- DFlash2 (architecture/dflash2.py, modules/arch_specific/dflash2.py): the drafter can attach to a
  tensor-parallel target when the experimental opt-in is set (experimental_tensor_parallel; --experimental-dflash2-tp
  in model_init, validated before any allocation: it needs --tensor_parallel and a separate drafter). The selector
  consumes precomputed paired (fp32 score, global int64 id) candidates (walk_candidates_block) instead of
  dense logits.
- Model.lm_head_topk, Model_TPMixin.tp_dispatch_lm_head_topk and mp_model_forward_lm_head_topk (model.py,
  model_tp.py, model_tp_fn.py): each TP rank crops its LM-head shard to the real vocabulary, applies the selector
  scale and softcap, takes a local top-k; the shards are gathered and merged (util/candidate_topk.py). Ties break
  deterministically: descending score, then ascending global token id (not the dense CUDA kernel's lane
  order). Adapted from the tp-mla work of Olt1z, as credited in the code.
- EXL3_TP_WORKER_TIMEOUT (default 20 seconds) sets how long the parent waits for TP worker replies, for cold
  Triton and compiled-tensor caches.
- util/tp_sharing.py: EXL3_TP_SHARING_STRATEGY (file_system by default, or file_descriptor on Linux) selects
  torch's multiprocessing sharing strategy for the parent and every rank; each rank prints a one-line JSON
  report (pid, descriptor limits, strategy) when it is set.
- util/tp_lazy_cache.py: experimental target-only host page tier for TP: per-rank pinned arenas allocated on
  overflow, with batched store/fetch transfer functions, used by the serving layer.

Upstream dev later added its own DFlash2 tensor-parallel support (dev commits 9cc3bd1 and e98785b); these
patches neither include nor depend on it. Tests: tests/tp_dflash_cpu and tests/tp_service_cpu.

